Internet is defined as network of networks

Packet Switching - Data transferred from one device to another device in form of packets and at destination all these packets will be re-assembled
and can be decoded

Data  from one device getting transferred to another device follows a set of rules called protocol.
IP - handles addressing and routing
TCP - ensures data packets are delivered correctly to receiver and is in proper order
Other protocols are UDP, HTTP, HTTPS etc

