Domain name - human readable address of website
Domain name system - finds IP address mapped to the domain name to display the website
DNS checks for cache- DNS Resolver-Root Server-TLD Server-Authoritive Server to search for the IP address mapped with the domain name for displaying
the website.

DNS resolver finds which app/website is running on which IP address and what records are mapped to it.
Types of records:
A record - Domain mapped to IPv4 address
AAAA record - Domain mapped to IPv6 address
CNAME - Alias for domain name
MX - Directs email to email Server
TXT - holds text for verification and additional info
NS - DNS entry that specifies which servers are authoritative for a domain. 
SOA - mandatory DNS record that holds essential administrative and technical information about a domain zone

