File/directory permissions:
drwxrwxr-x -> d stands for directory, rwx - owner, rwx - group, r-x - other
-rw-r--r-- -> - stands for file

chmod: to change permissions for files/directories, for user, group and others there are read, write and execute permissions-> r=4,w=2,x=1
eg: chmod 640 myfile.txt  - using numbers format
or using symbolic format
eg: chmod u+x myfile.txt

chmod -R 644 myfile.txt - to change permissions recursively in directories and subdirectories

chown: to change ownership of files/directories
chown var one.zip - owner has been changed
eg: -rwxr--r--. 1 var      ec2-user 1184280 Jul 22 06:32 one.zip

chown var:devops templatemo_629_nexus_system - owner and group both are changed
eg: drwxr-----. 2 var devops         6 Jul 22 06:41 templatemo_629_nexus_system

chown -R var:devops templatemo_629_nexus_system - to change ownership recursively in directories and subdirectories
chown 1001:1002 filename - we can change ownership using user ID and group ID also

chgrp: to change group ownership of files/directories
chgrp devops one.zip - to assign another group to file/directory
eg: -rwxr--r--. 1 var devops 1184280 Jul 22 06:32 one.zip

